---
/**
 * FourDimensionsFramework.astro — V4
 *
 * Overview diagram for the Four Dimensions of AI in Services framework
 * Whitney authored for the ai-lx (CarMax) workshop. This is the family
 * head — it sits above the per-dimension deep-dive components
 * (InteractionTypesDiagram / InteractionModelComparison and
 * CollaborationModelsDiagram) and gives the reader an immediate sense
 * of the framework's shape before they read the prose.
 *
 *   01 Actors         — relationship/network across two zones (Human / AI)
 *   02 Interface      — continuous horizontal spectrum (Explicit ↔ Ambient)
 *   03 Collaboration  — a set of four distinct structural shapes
 *   04 Control        — ordered five-step scale (Manual ↔ Autonomous)
 *
 * Layout: vertical stack of four full-width blocks. Each block has a
 * wide left rail (eyebrow + dimension name in Petrona display) and a
 * generous right area for a substantial inline-SVG graphic that
 * suggests the dimension's structural shape. Values are listed compactly
 * beneath each graphic in DM Sans body / DM Mono labels.
 *
 * Design rules: portfolio palette only (cream / warm-white / charcoal
 * family / gold family / sage family). Monochrome inline SVG, restrained
 * editorial register, no JS. Sibling visual vocabulary to
 * InteractionModelComparison.astro and CollaborationModelsDiagram.astro.
 *
 * This is v2 — the v1 attempt (PR #73) used a 2x2 layout with mini-glyphs
 * that read as gestural rather than substantive. v2 dedicates a full-width
 * row to each dimension so the graphics have room to breathe.
 */
---

<figure class="v4-fdf">
  <header class="v4-fdf-head">
    <span class="v4-fdf-section-eyebrow">Framework · four dimensions</span>
    <p class="v4-fdf-section-tagline">If the principles are where you're going, the dimensions are the levers, gears, and tools that get you there.</p>
  </header>

  <!-- ============================================================
       01 · ACTORS
       Two columns of named nodes (Human zone / AI zone) with faint
       relationship lines crossing the gap. Structural claim: this is
       a multi-actor system, not a single "the AI."
       ============================================================ -->
  <article class="v4-fdf-row v4-fdf-row--actors">
    <aside class="v4-fdf-rail">
      <span class="v4-fdf-eyebrow">01 / 04 · Actors</span>
      <h3 class="v4-fdf-name">Who is participating?</h3>
      <p class="v4-fdf-prompt">Two sides of the system. Naming them keeps the team from collapsing every AI into "the AI."</p>
    </aside>

    <div class="v4-fdf-body">
      <div class="v4-fdf-graphic">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 640 280" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Network of human-side and AI-side actors connected by relationships">
          <!-- Zone labels -->
          <text x="100" y="28" font-family="DM Mono, monospace" font-size="11" letter-spacing="0.18em" fill="var(--charcoal-soft)" text-anchor="middle">HUMAN SIDE</text>
          <text x="540" y="28" font-family="DM Mono, monospace" font-size="11" letter-spacing="0.18em" fill="var(--gold-text)" text-anchor="middle">AI SIDE</text>

          <!-- Zone divider rule (subtle vertical) -->
          <line x1="320" y1="50" x2="320" y2="260" stroke="var(--cream-deep)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 4"/>

          <!-- Relationship lines (drawn first so nodes sit on top) -->
          <!-- customer <-> personal AI -->
          <path d="M 160 80 Q 320 80 480 80" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1" fill="none" opacity="0.55"/>
          <!-- customer <-> customer-facing AI -->
          <path d="M 160 80 Q 320 130 480 140" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1" fill="none" opacity="0.4"/>
          <!-- front-stage assoc <-> customer-facing AI -->
          <path d="M 160 140 Q 320 140 480 140" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1" fill="none" opacity="0.55"/>
          <!-- front-stage assoc <-> employee-facing AI -->
          <path d="M 160 140 Q 320 180 480 200" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1" fill="none" opacity="0.4"/>
          <!-- back-stage assoc <-> employee-facing AI -->
          <path d="M 160 200 Q 320 200 480 200" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1" fill="none" opacity="0.55"/>
          <!-- supplier <-> supplier tools -->
          <path d="M 160 260 Q 320 260 480 260" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1" fill="none" opacity="0.55"/>
          <!-- back-stage assoc <-> supplier tools (cross-link) -->
          <path d="M 160 200 Q 320 240 480 260" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1" fill="none" opacity="0.3"/>

          <!-- HUMAN nodes (left column) -->
          <g font-family="DM Sans, sans-serif" font-size="12.5" fill="var(--charcoal)">
            <circle cx="100" cy="80" r="7" fill="var(--warm-white)" stroke="var(--charcoal-mid)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="118" y="84">Customer</text>

            <circle cx="100" cy="140" r="7" fill="var(--warm-white)" stroke="var(--charcoal-mid)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="118" y="144">Front-stage associate</text>

            <circle cx="100" cy="200" r="7" fill="var(--warm-white)" stroke="var(--charcoal-mid)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="118" y="204">Back-stage associate</text>

            <circle cx="100" cy="260" r="7" fill="var(--warm-white)" stroke="var(--charcoal-mid)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="118" y="264">Supplier</text>
          </g>

          <!-- AI nodes (right column) -->
          <g font-family="DM Sans, sans-serif" font-size="12.5" fill="var(--charcoal)">
            <rect x="473" y="73" width="14" height="14" rx="2" fill="var(--gold-pale)" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="495" y="84">Customer's personal AI</text>

            <rect x="473" y="133" width="14" height="14" rx="2" fill="var(--gold-pale)" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="495" y="144">Customer-facing AI</text>

            <rect x="473" y="193" width="14" height="14" rx="2" fill="var(--gold-pale)" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="495" y="204">Employee-facing AI</text>

            <rect x="473" y="253" width="14" height="14" rx="2" fill="var(--gold-pale)" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="495" y="264">Supplier's tools</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <p class="v4-fdf-caption">A near-future scenario worth pushing on: an agent of the customer negotiating with an agent of the company — on behalf of a person who isn't directly in the loop.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- ============================================================
       02 · INTERFACE
       Wide horizontal spectrum with a gradient from charcoal (explicit)
       to gold (ambient). Three labeled positions; examples below each.
       Structural claim: continuous range, not three buckets.
       ============================================================ -->
  <article class="v4-fdf-row v4-fdf-row--interface">
    <aside class="v4-fdf-rail">
      <span class="v4-fdf-eyebrow">02 / 04 · Interface</span>
      <h3 class="v4-fdf-name">What is the point of connection?</h3>
      <p class="v4-fdf-prompt">A continuous range. Most teams default to explicit because chatbots are the available metaphor.</p>
    </aside>

    <div class="v4-fdf-body">
      <div class="v4-fdf-graphic">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 640 220" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Spectrum from explicit to ambient interface, with mix as the overlap zone">
          <defs>
            <linearGradient id="fdf-iface-grad" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="0">
              <stop offset="0%" stop-color="var(--charcoal-mid)" stop-opacity="0.85"/>
              <stop offset="50%" stop-color="var(--gold)" stop-opacity="0.55"/>
              <stop offset="100%" stop-color="var(--gold)" stop-opacity="0.95"/>
            </linearGradient>
          </defs>

          <!-- Spectrum bar -->
          <rect x="40" y="70" width="560" height="32" rx="2" fill="url(#fdf-iface-grad)"/>

          <!-- Tick marks at the three positions -->
          <line x1="80" y1="62" x2="80" y2="110" stroke="var(--charcoal)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <line x1="320" y1="62" x2="320" y2="110" stroke="var(--charcoal)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <line x1="560" y1="62" x2="560" y2="110" stroke="var(--gold-text)" stroke-width="1.5"/>

          <!-- Position labels (above the bar) -->
          <text x="80" y="50" font-family="Petrona, Georgia, serif" font-size="18" font-weight="700" fill="var(--charcoal)" text-anchor="middle">Explicit</text>
          <text x="320" y="50" font-family="Petrona, Georgia, serif" font-size="18" font-weight="700" fill="var(--charcoal)" text-anchor="middle" font-style="italic">Mix</text>
          <text x="560" y="50" font-family="Petrona, Georgia, serif" font-size="18" font-weight="700" fill="var(--gold-text)" text-anchor="middle">Ambient</text>

          <!-- AI-presence axis label -->
          <text x="40" y="135" font-family="DM Mono, monospace" font-size="10" letter-spacing="0.16em" fill="var(--charcoal-soft)">AI PRESENCE  →</text>
          <text x="600" y="135" font-family="DM Mono, monospace" font-size="10" letter-spacing="0.16em" fill="var(--charcoal-soft)" text-anchor="end">FADES INTO THE ENVIRONMENT</text>

          <!-- Examples row -->
          <g font-family="DM Mono, monospace" font-size="10" letter-spacing="0.10em" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)" text-anchor="middle">
            <text x="80" y="170">CHATBOT</text>
            <text x="80" y="186">DASHBOARD</text>

            <text x="320" y="170">VOICE-LED CONCIERGE</text>
            <text x="320" y="186">WITH A VISIBLE TRANSCRIPT</text>

            <text x="560" y="170">LICENSE-PLATE READER</text>
            <text x="560" y="186">DOOR THAT GREETS BY NAME</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <p class="v4-fdf-caption">Ambient and mix are where service design has the most to say — and where teams have done the least practice.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- ============================================================
       03 · COLLABORATION
       Four distinct mini-shapes in a horizontal row. Same vocabulary
       as the deep-dive but compressed: just the shape and the name.
       Structural claim: these are FOUR different shapes, not variations
       on one.
       ============================================================ -->
  <article class="v4-fdf-row v4-fdf-row--collab">
    <aside class="v4-fdf-rail">
      <span class="v4-fdf-eyebrow">03 / 04 · Collaboration</span>
      <h3 class="v4-fdf-name">How does the work get done?</h3>
      <p class="v4-fdf-prompt">Four distinct patterns. Naming them opens the design space beyond the sequential default.</p>
    </aside>

    <div class="v4-fdf-body">
      <div class="v4-fdf-graphic v4-fdf-collab-strip">

        <!-- Sequential: zigzag -->
        <div class="v4-fdf-collab-cell">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 140 80" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Sequential — turns alternate between human and AI">
            <line x1="10" y1="20" x2="130" y2="20" stroke="var(--cream-deep)" stroke-width="1"/>
            <line x1="10" y1="60" x2="130" y2="60" stroke="var(--cream-deep)" stroke-width="1"/>
            <circle cx="22" cy="20" r="3.5" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)"/>
            <line x1="24" y1="22" x2="52" y2="58" stroke="var(--charcoal-mid)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <circle cx="54" cy="60" r="3.5" fill="var(--gold)"/>
            <line x1="56" y1="58" x2="84" y2="22" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <circle cx="86" cy="20" r="3.5" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)"/>
            <line x1="88" y1="22" x2="116" y2="58" stroke="var(--charcoal-mid)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <circle cx="118" cy="60" r="3.5" fill="var(--gold)"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="v4-fdf-collab-name">Sequential</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Parallel: two stacked tracks toward shared goal -->
        <div class="v4-fdf-collab-cell">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 140 80" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Parallel — both work toward a shared goal at different complexity levels">
            <line x1="10" y1="20" x2="100" y2="20" stroke="var(--charcoal-mid)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <circle cx="30" cy="20" r="2.5" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)"/>
            <circle cx="60" cy="20" r="2.5" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)"/>
            <circle cx="90" cy="20" r="2.5" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)"/>

            <line x1="10" y1="60" x2="100" y2="60" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <circle cx="30" cy="60" r="2.5" fill="var(--gold)"/>
            <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="2.5" fill="var(--gold)"/>
            <circle cx="90" cy="60" r="2.5" fill="var(--gold)"/>

            <circle cx="118" cy="40" r="10" fill="var(--gold-pale)" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <line x1="100" y1="20" x2="111" y2="34" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="1"/>
            <line x1="100" y1="60" x2="111" y2="46" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="1"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="v4-fdf-collab-name">Parallel</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Independent: closed loop, no human -->
        <div class="v4-fdf-collab-cell">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 140 80" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Independent — AI operates alone in a closed loop">
            <circle cx="70" cy="40" r="26" fill="none" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/>
            <rect x="58" y="28" width="24" height="24" rx="3" fill="var(--gold-pale)" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <text x="70" y="44" text-anchor="middle" font-family="DM Mono, monospace" font-size="8.5" fill="var(--gold-text)" letter-spacing="0.06em">AI</text>
            <polygon points="92,40 96,46 100,40 96,34" fill="var(--gold)"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="v4-fdf-collab-name">Independent</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Orchestrated: constellation -->
        <div class="v4-fdf-collab-cell">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 140 80" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Orchestrated — multiple actors coordinated across a journey">
            <path d="M 20 40 Q 50 14 70 22" fill="none" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1"/>
            <path d="M 70 22 Q 95 14 120 40" fill="none" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1"/>
            <path d="M 20 40 Q 50 66 70 58" fill="none" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1"/>
            <path d="M 70 58 Q 95 66 120 40" fill="none" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1"/>

            <circle cx="20" cy="40" r="7" fill="var(--warm-white)" stroke="var(--charcoal-mid)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <rect x="63" y="15" width="14" height="14" rx="2" fill="var(--gold-pale)" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <polygon points="70,52 78,60 70,68 62,60" fill="var(--warm-white)" stroke="var(--charcoal-mid)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
            <circle cx="120" cy="40" r="7" fill="var(--warm-white)" stroke="var(--charcoal-mid)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="v4-fdf-collab-name">Orchestrated</span>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p class="v4-fdf-caption">Most teams describe AI work as sequential by default. Naming the other three opens the design space.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- ============================================================
       04 · CONTROL
       Five-step ordered scale, each step a small "human + AI" pairing
       where the proportions shift. Connected by a horizontal axis with
       ticks. Structural claim: this is an ORDERED scale, not a set.
       ============================================================ -->
  <article class="v4-fdf-row v4-fdf-row--control">
    <aside class="v4-fdf-rail">
      <span class="v4-fdf-eyebrow">04 / 04 · Control</span>
      <h3 class="v4-fdf-name">How much autonomy does the AI have?</h3>
      <p class="v4-fdf-prompt">An ordered five-step scale. "Use AI" is never a binary — every position has consequences for trust, liability, recovery, and brand.</p>
    </aside>

    <div class="v4-fdf-body">
      <div class="v4-fdf-graphic">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 640 260" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Five-step ordered scale from manual to autonomous; human share shrinks as AI share grows">

          <!-- Background axis -->
          <line x1="60" y1="200" x2="600" y2="200" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <!-- Ticks -->
          <line x1="80" y1="196" x2="80" y2="208" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <line x1="200" y1="196" x2="200" y2="208" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <line x1="320" y1="196" x2="320" y2="208" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <line x1="440" y1="196" x2="440" y2="208" stroke="var(--charcoal-soft)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <line x1="560" y1="196" x2="560" y2="208" stroke="var(--gold-text)" stroke-width="2"/>
          <!-- Direction arrow at end -->
          <polygon points="600,200 590,194 590,206" fill="var(--gold-text)"/>

          <!-- Axis labels -->
          <text x="60" y="232" font-family="DM Mono, monospace" font-size="10" letter-spacing="0.16em" fill="var(--charcoal-soft)">HUMAN DOES THE WORK</text>
          <text x="600" y="232" font-family="DM Mono, monospace" font-size="10" letter-spacing="0.16em" fill="var(--gold-text)" text-anchor="end">AI DOES THE WORK</text>

          <!-- Step 1: MANUAL — full human, no AI -->
          <g>
            <!-- Human bar: tall -->
            <rect x="68" y="80" width="24" height="110" rx="2" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)"/>
            <!-- AI bar: invisible / 0 -->
            <line x1="95" y1="188" x2="119" y2="188" stroke="var(--cream-deep)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <text x="80" y="68" font-family="DM Mono, monospace" font-size="9" letter-spacing="0.12em" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)" text-anchor="middle">01</text>
            <text x="80" y="252" font-family="Petrona, Georgia, serif" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="var(--charcoal)" text-anchor="middle">Manual</text>
          </g>

          <!-- Step 2: ASSISTED — human reviews every output -->
          <g>
            <rect x="188" y="105" width="24" height="85" rx="2" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)"/>
            <rect x="215" y="160" width="24" height="30" rx="2" fill="var(--gold)" opacity="0.85"/>
            <text x="200" y="68" font-family="DM Mono, monospace" font-size="9" letter-spacing="0.12em" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)" text-anchor="middle">02</text>
            <text x="213" y="252" font-family="Petrona, Georgia, serif" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="var(--charcoal)" text-anchor="middle">Assisted</text>
          </g>

          <!-- Step 3: MONITORED — AI runs continuously, human reviews on a schedule -->
          <g>
            <rect x="308" y="135" width="24" height="55" rx="2" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)"/>
            <rect x="335" y="120" width="24" height="70" rx="2" fill="var(--gold)" opacity="0.85"/>
            <text x="320" y="68" font-family="DM Mono, monospace" font-size="9" letter-spacing="0.12em" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)" text-anchor="middle">03</text>
            <text x="333" y="252" font-family="Petrona, Georgia, serif" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="var(--charcoal)" text-anchor="middle">Monitored</text>
          </g>

          <!-- Step 4: AUTOMATED — AI acts, humans pulled in on exception -->
          <g>
            <rect x="428" y="160" width="24" height="30" rx="2" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)"/>
            <rect x="455" y="100" width="24" height="90" rx="2" fill="var(--gold)" opacity="0.9"/>
            <text x="440" y="68" font-family="DM Mono, monospace" font-size="9" letter-spacing="0.12em" fill="var(--charcoal-mid)" text-anchor="middle">04</text>
            <text x="453" y="252" font-family="Petrona, Georgia, serif" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="var(--charcoal)" text-anchor="middle">Automated</text>
          </g>

          <!-- Step 5: AUTONOMOUS — AI alone unless severe failure -->
          <g>
            <line x1="548" y1="188" x2="572" y2="188" stroke="var(--cream-deep)" stroke-width="2"/>
            <rect x="575" y="80" width="24" height="110" rx="2" fill="var(--gold)"/>
            <text x="560" y="68" font-family="DM Mono, monospace" font-size="9" letter-spacing="0.12em" fill="var(--gold-text)" text-anchor="middle">05</text>
            <text x="573" y="252" font-family="Petrona, Georgia, serif" font-size="14" font-weight="700" fill="var(--gold-text)" text-anchor="middle">Autonomous</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <p class="v4-fdf-caption">Adapted from the U.S. military's human-in-the-loop / on-the-loop / out-of-the-loop taxonomy, translated into a five-step service design vocabulary.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <figcaption class="v4-fdf-footer">
    Four dimensions, one framework. Most existing AI vocabulary is interface-level; this is the set a service designer can actually turn.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .v4-fdf {
    margin: 3rem 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .v4-fdf-head {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .v4-fdf-section-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, 'DM Mono', monospace);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold-text, #8A6820);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .v4-fdf-section-tagline {
    font-family: var(--font-display, 'Petrona', Georgia, serif);
    font-size: 18px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--charcoal, #2A2520);
    margin: 6px 0 0 0;
    max-width: none;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  /* ====== Row (one per dimension) ====== */
  .v4-fdf-row {
    background: var(--cream, #F4EDE4);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold, #C8943E);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 2rem 2rem 2.25rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(220px, 1fr) minmax(0, 2.4fr);
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* ====== Left rail (eyebrow + dimension name + prompt) ====== */
  .v4-fdf-rail {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .v4-fdf-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, 'DM Mono', monospace);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold-text, #8A6820);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .v4-fdf-name {
    font-family: var(--font-display, 'Petrona', Georgia, serif);
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--charcoal, #2A2520);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .v4-fdf-prompt {
    font-family: var(--font-body, 'DM Sans', sans-serif);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--charcoal-mid, #4A443D);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 32ch;
  }

  /* ====== Right body (graphic + caption) ====== */
  .v4-fdf-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .v4-fdf-graphic {
    background: var(--warm-white, #FAF7F3);
    border: 1px solid var(--cream-deep, #EBE1D4);
    border-radius: 3px;
